  "about": "The prompt stamp: the executor's hook (internal/hook) runs these cases. A case plays its steps in order against one state directory, with the clock at now plus at seconds in the zone offset seconds east of UTC. A step is an event — UserPromptSubmit when none is named — with the payload of the session, or input as a raw text. state is the snapshot the step finds: the name of one of snapshots, with set laid over it (a dotted path, a list index as a number), an object as it is, null for a file that reads null, raw for a text, none for no file; a step without state finds the snapshot of the step before it. guards is guards.tsv of the host, none for no file; env is laid over an environment without CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR. says is the context the hook adds, line by line, null for nothing printed. throttle is the throttle file of the session after the step, mark the mark of what its conversation was told of its role, null for none, listing the names in the state directory; files are files of the state directory as the case finds them, aged that many seconds.",
